ourse of their various business activities, such parties and their respective affiliates may make or hold a broad array of investments and actively trade debt and equity securities (or related derivative securities) and financial instruments (including bank loans) for their own account and for the accounts of their customers, and such investments and securities activities may involve the Company’s securities and/or instruments.","section":"ITEM 16. FORM 10-K SUMMARY.","block":1544,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-017085","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-18","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001693256","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1693256/000110465926017085/wttr-20251231x10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/bb3133d02453b8a6604827f2a9d4fd56322e7bf13941e41aa7e494d5a2667f53.bin","sha256":"bb3133d02453b8a6604827f2a9d4fd56322e7bf13941e41aa7e494d5a2667f53"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"managementExplanations":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"1d80269ffb5c73126da5da1da9d0107dae6ba9935b6b05cdfa3cb02d5b5e72bf","quote":"●Political instability or armed conflict, including in crude oil or natural gas producing regions and OPEC+ policy decisions.","context":"●Our business depends on capital spending by the oil and gas industry in the U.S. and reductions in capital spending could have a material adverse effect on our liquidity, results of operations and financial condition.","section":"●Our business depends on capital spending by the oil and gas industry in the U.S. and reductions in capital spending could have a material adverse effect on our liquidity, results of operations and financial condition.","block":186,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-017085","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-18","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001693256","url":"ht